       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Acetaminophen 5000 mg three times daily comes to 15 g/day, nearly four times the usual maximum of 4 g/day. A single 5 g dose is also above the normal maximum single dose of 1 g. At this level the risk of acute liver failure is serious, even with normal liver function. Many institutions cap adults at 3 to 4 g/day.\n\nMaybe you meant one of these:\n- **500 mg** three times daily (1.5 g/day)\n- **650 mg** three times daily (about 2 g/day)\n- **1000 mg** three times daily (3 g/day), which is a common full-strength regimen\n- **5000 mg total per day**, split into smaller doses, which would still be above the usual limit\n\nIf you want the dose as written, tell me it's intentional and give me the clinical rationale. I'd still suggest checking it with pharmacy first. Otherwise, tell me the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it right away."
